With the decision by the NCAA to allow teams to expand to a 12-game schedule, Texas added [[NCAA Division I Football Championship Subdivision|Division I-AA]] Sam Houston State to its schedule.<ref name="Bearkats">{{cite news |url=http://www.chron.com/disp/story.mpl/sports/fb/fbc/4217367.html|title=Bearkats are dreaming the impossible dream|author=Duarte, Joseph|newspaper=[[Houston Chronicle]]|date=September 27, 2006|access-date=January 26, 2011}}</ref> The game was the first UT game since 2004 not to be televised nationally on broadcast or cable, though it was available on [[pay per view]] from [[DirecTV]] and [[Dish Network]].<ref name="Bearkats"/> This was the first-ever meeting of the Texas Longhorns and the Sam Houston State Bearkats and the first time Texas played a Division I-AA team in fourteen years.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/ncaa/football/recap?gid=200609300083&prov=ap|title=No. 7 Texas 56, Sam Houston State 3|author=Vertino, Jim|work=[[Yahoo! Sports]]|agency=[[Associated Press]]|date=September 30, 2006|access-date=January 26, 2011}}</ref>

Texas won the game 56–3.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.espn.com/college-football/playbyplay?gameId=262730251|title=Sam Houston State 3, Texas 56 – Play-by-Play|publisher=[[ESPN]]|date=September 23, 2006|access-date=January 26, 2011}}</ref>

